insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain advanced javascript concepts in your own words.","Recognise and apply: prototypes let objects share methods without copying them.","Recognise and apply: debounce and throttle control how often expensive work runs.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers advanced javascript concepts: closures in depth, prototypes, the event loop, and writing robust code. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that prototypes let objects share methods without copying them. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that debounce and throttle control how often expensive work runs. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how advanced javascript concepts fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'javascript', 'function debounce(fn, wait) {
